━━━ stdout
Create and enable platform configuration files in `.opentide/configurations/platforms/`.

␛[1m␛[4mUsage:␛[0m ␛[1mopentide setup platforms␛[0m [OPTIONS]

␛[1m␛[4mOptions:␛[0m
  ␛[1m-C␛[0m, ␛[1m--path␛[0m <PATH_FLAG>
          Repository path
          
          [default: .]

      ␛[1m--sentinel␛[0m
          Enable Microsoft Sentinel

      ␛[1m--defender-for-endpoint␛[0m
          Enable Microsoft Defender for Endpoint

      ␛[1m--splunk␛[0m
          Enable Splunk Enterprise Security

      ␛[1m--sentinel-one␛[0m
          Enable SentinelOne

      ␛[1m--crowdstrike␛[0m
          Enable CrowdStrike Falcon

      ␛[1m--harfanglab␛[0m
          Enable HarfangLab

      ␛[1m--carbon-black-cloud␛[0m
          Enable Carbon Black Cloud

      ␛[1m--elastic␛[0m
          Enable Elastic Security

      ␛[1m--sysdig␛[0m
          Enable Sysdig Secure (Falco)

      ␛[1m--bitdefender␛[0m
          Enable Bitdefender GravityZone

      ␛[1m--graylog␛[0m
          Enable Graylog

      ␛[1m--exabeam␛[0m
          Enable Exabeam New-Scale SIEM

      ␛[1m--google-secops␛[0m
          Enable Google Security Operations (YARA-L)

      ␛[1m--plan␛[0m
          List the files each step would write, and write nothing

  ␛[1m-y␛[0m, ␛[1m--yes␛[0m
          Write without asking for confirmation

      ␛[1m--help␛[0m
          Print help

Examples:
  $ opentide setup platforms --sentinel --splunk --yes

